Timeline
- Read docs/media (record_casts.sh, pty_drive.py, README): asciinema 3.2.1
  --headless -f asciicast-v2 + agg 1.9.0 (asciinema-agg). Reused as-is.
- Server has no bot; the bot runs offline and its inputs become a trace
  (digest_every 1) that Emacs replays through the lockstep server.
- s.lines is per level (resets at level-up), so the switch from bot to
  hard drops is by frame (540), not by lines. Searched 11 seeds x 3
  switches; picked seed 42 (docs continuity), 923 frames, 30.8 s.
- Take 1: synchronous prefetch left ~13 s idle; agg's idle limit then
  squeezed the game's 5 s white wait too. Take 2: unpaced streaming
  starved redisplay (frame 100 received at 2.2 s, shown at 16.2 s).
  Take 3: controller-paced ticks, 0 stalls. Take 4 (load 5.4): 24 stalls;
  lead 30 -> 90 frames and gc-cons-threshold 64 MB. Take 5: 0 stalls.
- xterm.el's terminal queries cost 2 s each against a headless recorder;
  a throwaway init dir sets xterm-query-timeout nil before tty init.
- Per user direction: no patch to tetris-mit-display.el; only the existing
  option tetris-mit-cell-string is set (3 spaces), and a header line.
- Verified frames of the GIF visually (stdlib GIF decoder -> PNG): the
  countdown, play, the game-over fill, game 2's countdown, the PASS summary.

